vectorwake (criccomini, push to main): a Subspace-inspired MMO with our own art. Deterministic C99 core, Rust authoritative server, Defold client. Zones own their rules and send them over the wire: one weapon model, a tech tree, bounty derived from what you hold.                        
Faithfulness to the original settled the numbers, the map, and mobile controls; then vectorwake shipped to Vultr and playing it found what no check could.                                                                                                                                     
From quietly broken fleet to a real game: live failures swept, offline mode gone, bots live and wall-wise, detailed hulls on converted maps, new interface and sound, then one huge polish day: the Safari saga, explosions, rung colors, field doors, teams designed, alpha at 10.            
Four days making the game legible and then polished: a clear field, fire heard off snapshot counts, a rail-and-stage menu that explains itself with drawn keys, death cards and hover names, one helmet for pilots and bots, smoothed remote ships, and bots that unstick themselves.          
